  ["background.house-lyrandar-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Lyrandar Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["background.house-medani-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Medani Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["magicitem.house-of-cards.bmt2014"]={title="House of Cards",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis deck of cards is decorated with geometric shapes that have a protective motif. While you're holding the deck, you can use an action to shuffle it and cause the cards to deal themselves out and transform into a shelter made of cards. The shelter can be shaped however you desire, but it must fit in a 40-foot cube centered on a point within 30 feet of you. The shelter has one door and up to four windows, and only you can open or close them. It has a floor and a roof, and it maintains a comfortable temperature inside.\n\nThe shelter has AC 15, 50 hit points, and immunity to poison and psychic damage. The shelter lasts for 24 hours, until you dismiss it as an action, or until it is reduced to 0 hit points. When the shelter's duration ends, it transforms back into a deck of cards and appears in your hand. Once the deck has transformed into a shelter, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["background.house-orien-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Orien Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["background.house-phiarlan-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Phiarlan Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["background.house-sivis-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Sivis Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["background.house-tharashk-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Tharashk Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["background.house-thuranni-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Thuranni Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 32\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["background.house-vadalis-heir.efa2014"]={title="House Vadalis Heir",subtitle="Background - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["creature.howler.mpmm2014"]={title="Howler",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 155\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 5 | WIS 14 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nA howler has advantage on attack rolls against a creature if at least one of the howler's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe howler makes two Rending Bite attacks.\n\nRending Bite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage, plus 22 (4d10) psychic damage if the target is frightened. This attack ignores damage resistance.\n\nMind-Breaking Howl {@recharge 4}\n\nThe howler emits a keening howl in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 13 Wisdom saving throw or take 16 (3d10) psychic damage and be frightened until the end of the howler's next turn. While a creature is frightened in this way, its speed is halved, and it is incapacitated. A target that successfully saves is immune to the Mind-Breaking Howl of all howlers for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.howler.mtf2014"]={title="Howler",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 210\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 90 (12d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 5 | WIS 20 | CHA 6\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal but can't speak\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPack Tactics\n\nA howler has advantage on attack rolls against a creature if at least one of the howler's allies is within 5 feet of the creature and the ally isn't incapacitated.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe howler makes two bite attacks.\n\nRending Bite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage. If the target is frightened it takes an additional 22 (4d10) psychic damage. This attack ignores damage resistance.\n\nMind-Breaking Howl {@recharge}\n\nThe howler emits a keening howl in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in that area that isn't deafened must succeed on a 16 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened until the end of the howler's next turn. While a creature is frightened in this way, its speed is halved, and it is incapacitated. A target that successfully saves is immune to the Mind-Breaking Howl of all howlers for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.howling-hatred-initiate.pota2014"]={title="Howling Hatred Initiate",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 9 (2d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 9 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGuiding Wind (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nAs a bonus action, the initiate gains advantage on the next ranged attack roll it makes before the end of its next turn.\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe initiate can hold its breath for 30 minutes.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.howling-hatred-priest.pota2014"]={title="Howling Hatred Priest",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 190\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 45 (10d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 16 | CON 10 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Auran, Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nHold Breath\n\nThe priest can hold its breath for 30 minutes.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe priest makes two melee attacks or two ranged attacks.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage."},
  ["traphazard.howling-wind.fraif2014"]={title="Howling Wind",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - FRAiF - 2014",body="Pagina: 96\n\nIcewind Dale's winds can reach incredible pitch and volume, making it impossible to hear. Creatures outdoors in howling winds have the XPHB condition."},
  ["creature.hrabbaz.wdh2014"]={title="Hrabbaz",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 17 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 12\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Orc\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nIndomitable (2/Day)\n\nHrabbaz can reroll a saving throw that he fails. He must use the new roll.\n\nRelentless Endurance (Recharges after a Long Rest)\n\nWhen Hrabbaz is reduced to 0 hit points but not killed outright, he drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nHrabbaz makes three attacks with his morningstar.\n\nMorningstar\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) piercing damage, plus 3 (1d6) piercing damage if Hrabbaz has more than half his hit points remaining."},
  ["creature.hrigg-roundrook.dsotdq2014"]={title="Hrigg Roundrook",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 211\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Dwarvish\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBonus Proficiencies\n\nHrigg is proficient with simple and martial weapons and light and medium armor.\n\nDwarven Resilience\n\nHrigg has advantage on saving throws made to avoid or end the poisoned condition on himself.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMaul\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.hrossk.wdmm2014"]={title="Hrossk",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 183\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["deity.hruggek.phb2014"]={title="Hruggek",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["creature.huge-giant-crab.tftyp2014"]={title="Huge Giant Crab",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 103\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 161 (14d12 + 70)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 15 | CON 20 | INT 1 | WIS 9 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBanded Claw\n\nOn one of its claws, the crab wears a rune-covered copper band that makes it immune to being charmed, frightened, and paralyzed. The copper band is worthless as a treasure, as the magic is keyed to this crab.\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe crab can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h27 (4d10 + 5) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled, escape 14. The crab has two claws, each of which can grapple only one target."},
  ["creature.huge-gray-ooze.wdmm2014"]={title="Huge Gray Ooze",subtitle="Criatura - WDMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: H\n\nCR: 8\n\nPV: 152 (16d12 + 48)\n\nSTR 18\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nAs an action, it can make two attacks with its pseudopods.\n\nPseudopod\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h21 (6d6) acid damage, or 42 (12d6) acid damage while the ooze is enlarged. If the target is wearing nonmagical metal armor, its armor is partly corroded and takes a permanent and cumulative −1 penalty to the AC it offers. The armor is destroyed if the penalty reduces its AC to 10.\n\nEnlarge (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nFor 1 minute, the ooze magically increases in size. While enlarged, the ooze is Gargantuan, doubles its damage dice with its pseudopod attack, and makes Strength checks and Strength saving throws with advantage.\n\nInvisibility (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe ooze magically turns invisible for up to 1 hour until it attacks, it uses its Enlarge, or its concentration is broken (as if concentration on a spell)."},
  ["creature.huge-ochre-jelly.tftyp2014"]={title="Huge Ochre Jelly",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 225\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: H\n\nPV: 51 (6d12 + 12)"},
  ["creature.huge-polar-bear.tftyp2014"]={title="Huge Polar Bear",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 187\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: H\n\nPV: 65 (5d12 + 15)"},
  ["creature.huge-stone-golem.skt2014"]={title="Huge Stone Golem",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 153\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: H\n\nPV: 195 (17d12 + 85)"},
  ["creature.hulgaz.bmt2014"]={title="Hulgaz",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 169\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / L\n\nCR: 14\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 190 (20d10 + 80)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 17 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 14 | WIS 15 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: acid, cold\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Hulgaz fails a saving throw, she can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nHulgaz has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nHulgaz makes two Claw attacks and one Intoxicating Sting attack.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nIntoxicating Sting\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one creature. h8 (1d10 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 17 Wisdom saving throw or have the charmed condition until the start of Hulgaz's next turn.\n\nBrimstone Vapor {@recharge 5}\n\nHulgaz exhales a 30-foot cone of noxious, scorching-hot vapor. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 17 Constitution saving throw or have the poisoned condition for 1 minute. While poisoned in this way, a creature takes 31 (7d8) fire damage at the start of each of its turns and has disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws. A target can repeat the Constitution saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nHulgaz makes one Claw attack.\n\nCharm\n\nHulgaz uses Spellcasting to cast Charm Person.\n\nCurdle Heart (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nHulgaz sours the good feelings of her charmed victims. She chooses any number of creatures she can see who are charmed by her. Each target takes 17 (5d6) psychic damage as the charmed condition applied by Hulgaz ends on it."},
  ["creature.hulil-lutan.egw2014"]={title="Hulil Lutan",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 240\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 15"},
  ["creature.hulking-crab.skt2014"]={title="Hulking Crab",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 240\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / H\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 76 (8d12 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 8 | CON 16 | INT 3 | WIS 11 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 30 ft.\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe crab can breathe air and water.\n\nShell Camouflage\n\nWhile the crab remains motionless with its eyestalks and pincers tucked close to its body, it resembles a natural formation or a pile of detritus. A creature within 30 feet of it can discern its true nature with a successful 15 Intelligence (Nature) check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe crab makes two attacks with its claws.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h20 (3d10 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 15). The crab has two claws, each of which can grapple only one target"},
  ["creature.hulking-shadow.dsotdq2014"]={title="Hulking Shadow",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 174\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead"},
  ["species.human.phb2014"]={title="Human",subtitle="Especie - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\nAge\n\nHumans reach adulthood in their late teens and live less than a century.\n\nSize\n\nHumans vary widely in height and build, from barely 5 feet to well over 6 feet tall. Regardless of your position in that range, your size is Medium.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and one extra language of your choice. Humans typically learn the languages of other peoples they deal with, including obscure dialects. They are fond of sprinkling their speech with words borrowed from other tongues: Orc curses, Elvish musical expressions, Dwarvish military phrases, and so on."},
  ["species.human.xphb2024"]={title="Human",subtitle="Especie - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 194\n\nResourceful\n\nYou gain XPHB whenever you finish a XPHB.\n\nSkillful\n\nYou gain proficiency in one skill of your choice.\n\nVersatile\n\nYou gain an feats of your choice."},
  ["species.human-innistrad.psi2014"]={title="Human (Innistrad)",subtitle="Especie - PSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 8\n\nAge\n\nHumans reach adulthood in their late teens and live less than a century.\n\nAlignment\n\nHumans tend toward no particular alignment.\n\nSize\n\nHumans vary widely in height and build, from barely 5 feet to well over 6 feet tall. Regardless of your position in that range, your size is Medium.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write Common and one extra language of your choice."},
  ["species.human-ixalan.psx2014"]={title="Human (Ixalan)",subtitle="Especie - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 11"},
  ["species.human-kaladesh.psk2014"]={title="Human (Kaladesh)",subtitle="Especie - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 22"},
  ["species.human-zendikar.psz2014"]={title="Human (Zendikar)",subtitle="Especie - PSZ - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["creature.humanoid-mutate.pabtso2014"]={title="Humanoid Mutate",subtitle="Criatura - PaBTSO - 2014",body="Pagina: 212\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 65 (10d8 + 20)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 15\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the mutate has disadvantage on attack rolls.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe mutate makes two Unarmed Strike or Nightmare Blast attacks.\n\nUnarmed Strike\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) bludgeoning damage plus 10 (3d6) psychic damage.\n\nNightmare Blast\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h7 (2d6) psychic damage, and the target must succeed on a 12 Wisdom saving throw or have the frightened condition until the start of the mutate's next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDefensive Flight\n\nImmediately after taking damage, the mutate flies up to its speed. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks."},
  ["creature.hundred-handed-one.mot2014"]={title="Hundred-Handed One",subtitle="Criatura - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 225\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: giant / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 243 (18d12 + 126)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 15 | CON 25 | INT 14 | WIS 16 | CHA 16\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Giant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nReactive\n\nThe giant can take one reaction on every turn in a combat.\n\nVigilant\n\nThe giant can't be surprised.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe giant makes four longsword attacks or two rock attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 13 to hit, reach 15 ft., one target. h21 (3d8 + 8) slashing damage.\n\nRock\n\nrw 13 to hit, range 60/240 ft., one target. h30 (4d10 + 8) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 21 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nDeflect Attack\n\nThe giant adds 5 to its AC against one weapon attack that would hit it. To do so, the giant must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["spell.hunger-of-hadar.phb2014"]={title="Hunger of Hadar",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 251\n\nYou open a gateway to the dark between the stars, a region infested with unknown horrors. A 20-foot-radius sphere of blackness and bitter cold appears, centered on a point within range and lasting for the duration. This void is filled with a cacophony of soft whispers and slurping noises that can be heard up to 30 feet away. No light, magical or otherwise, can illuminate the area, and creatures fully within the area are blinded.\n\nThe void creates a warp in the fabric of space, and the area is difficult terrain. Any creature that starts its turn in the area takes 2d6 cold damage. Any creature that ends its turn in the area must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 2d6 acid damage as milky, otherworldly tentacles rub against it."},
  ["spell.hunger-of-hadar.xphb2024"]={title="Hunger of Hadar",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 286\n\nYou open a gateway to the Far Realm, a region infested with unspeakable horrors. A 20-foot-radius XPHB of XPHB appears, centered on a point within range and lasting for the duration. The XPHB is XPHB, and it is filled with strange whispers and slurping noises, which can be heard up to 30 feet away. No light, magical or otherwise, can illuminate the area, and creatures fully within it have the XPHB condition.\n\nAny creature that starts its turn in the area takes 2d6 Cold damage. Any creature that ends its turn there must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or take 2d6 Acid damage from otherworldly tentacles."},
  ["feature.hungering-might.rhw2014.ranger.hollow-warden.7"]={title="Hungering Might",subtitle="Caracteristica - RHW - 2014",body=""},
  ["creature.hungry-ghast.cos2014"]={title="Hungry Ghast",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.hungry-sorrowsworn.mpmm2014"]={title="Hungry Sorrowsworn",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 223\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 225 (30d8 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 6 | WIS 11 | CHA 6\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLife Hunger\n\nIf a creature within 60 feet of the sorrowsworn regains hit points, the sorrowsworn gains two benefits until the end of its next turn: it has advantage on attack rolls, and its Bite deals an extra 22 (4d10) necrotic damage on a hit.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sorrowsworn makes one Bite attack and one Claw attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) piercing damage plus 13 (3d8) necrotic damage.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h18 (4d6 + 4) slashing damage. If the target is Medium or smaller, it is grappled (escape 16), and it is restrained until the grapple ends. While grappling a creature, the sorrowsworn can't make a Claw attack."},
  ["item.hunk-of-cheese.phb2014"]={title="Hunk of Cheese",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 158\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["subclass.hunter.phb2014.ranger.hunter.0"]={title="Hunter",subtitle="Subclasse - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 3 - Colossus Slayer\n\nPagina: 93\n\nYour tenacity can wear down the most potent foes. When you hit a creature with a weapon attack, the creature takes an extra 1d8 damage if it's below its hit point maximum. You can deal this extra damage only once per turn.\n\nNivel 3 - Giant Killer\n\nPagina: 93\n\nWhen a Large or larger creature within 5 feet of you hits or misses you with an attack, you can use your reaction to attack that creature immediately after its attack, provided that you can see the creature.\n\nNivel 3 - Horde Breaker\n\nPagina: 93\n\nOnce on each of your turns when you make a weapon attack, you can make another attack with the same weapon against a different creature that is within 5 feet of the original target and within range of your weapon.\n\nNivel 3 - Hunter\n\nPagina: 93\n\nEmulating the Hunter archetype means accepting your place as a bulwark between civilization and the terrors of the wilderness. As you walk the Hunter's path, you learn specialized techniques for fighting the threats you face, from rampaging ogres and hordes of orcs to towering giants and terrifying dragons.\n\nNivel 3 - Hunter\n\nPagina: 127\n\nProtect Nature and People from Destruction\n\nYou stalk prey in the wilds and elsewhere, using your abilities as a Hunter to protect nature and people everywhere from forces that would destroy them.\n\nNivel 3 - Hunter's Lore\n\nPagina: 127\n\nYou can call on the forces of nature to reveal certain strengths and weaknesses of your prey. While a creature is marked by your Hunter's Mark, you know whether that creature has any Immunities, Resistances, or Vulnerabilities, and if the creature has any, you know what they are.\n\nNivel 3 - Hunter's Prey\n\nPagina: 93\n\nAt 3rd level, you gain one of the following features of your choice.\n\nNivel 3 - Hunter's Prey\n\nPagina: 127\n\nYou gain one of the following feature options of your choice. Whenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB, you can replace the chosen option with the other one.\n\nColossus Slayer\n\nYour tenacity can wear down even the most resilient foes. When you hit a creature with a weapon, the weapon deals an extra 1d8 damage to the target if it's missing any of its XPHB. You can deal this extra damage only once per turn.\n\nHorde Breaker\n\nOnce on each of your turns when you make an attack with a weapon, you can make another attack with the same weapon against a different creature that is within 5 feet of the original target, that is within the weapon's range, and that you haven't attacked this turn.\n\nNivel 3 - Hunter's Prey\n\nNivel 7 - Defensive Tactics\n\nPagina: 93\n\nAt 7th level, you gain one of the following features of your choice.\n\nNivel 7 - Defensive Tactics\n\nPagina: 127\n\nYou gain one of the following feature options of your choice. Whenever you finish a XPHB or XPHB, you can replace the chosen option with the other one.\n\nEscape the Horde\n\nXPHB have XPHB against you.\n\nMultiattack Defense\n\nWhen a creature hits you with an attack roll, that creature has XPHB on all other attack rolls against you this turn.\n\nNivel 7 - Defensive Tactics\n\nNivel 7 - Escape the Horde\n\nPagina: 93\n\nOpportunity attacks against you are made with disadvantage.\n\nNivel 7 - Multiattack Defense\n\nPagina: 93\n\nWhen a creature hits you with an attack, you gain a +4 bonus to AC against all subsequent attacks made by that creature for the rest of the turn.\n\nNivel 7 - Steel Will\n\nPagina: 93\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nNivel 11 - Multiattack\n\nPagina: 93\n\nAt 11th level, you gain one of the following features of your choice.\n\nNivel 11 - Superior Hunter's Prey\n\nPagina: 127\n\nOnce per turn when you deal damage to a creature marked by your Hunter's Mark, you can also deal that spell's extra damage to a different creature that you can see within 30 feet of the first creature.\n\nNivel 11 - Superior Hunter's Prey\n\nNivel 11 - Volley\n\nPagina: 93\n\nYou can use your action to make a ranged attack against any number of creatures within 10 feet of a point you can see within your weapon's range. You must have ammunition for each target, as normal, and you make a separate attack roll for each target.\n\nNivel 11 - Whirlwind Attack\n\nPagina: 93\n\nYou can use your action to make a melee attack against any number of creatures within 5 feet of you, with a separate attack roll for each target.\n\nNivel 15 - Evasion\n\nPagina: 93\n\nYou can nimbly dodge out of the way of certain area effects, such as a red dragon's fiery breath or a lightning bolt spell. When you are subjected to an effect that allows you to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half damage, you instead take no damage if you succeed on the saving throw, and only half damage if you fail.\n\nNivel 15 - Stand Against the Tide\n\nPagina: 93\n\nWhen a hostile creature misses you with a melee attack, you can use your reaction to force that creature to repeat the same attack against another creature (other than itself) of your choice.\n\nNivel 15 - Superior Hunter's Defense\n\nPagina: 93\n\nAt 15th level, you gain one of the following features of your choice.\n\nNivel 15 - Superior Hunter's Defense\n\nPagina: 127\n\nWhen you take damage, you can take a XPHB to give yourself XPHB to that damage and any other damage of the same type until the end of the current turn.\n\nNivel 15 - Superior Hunter's Defense\n\nNivel 15 - Uncanny Dodge\n\nPagina: 93\n\nWhen an attacker that you can see hits you with an attack, you can use your reaction to halve the attack's damage against you."},
  ["feature.hunter.phb2014.ranger.hunter.3"]={title="Hunter",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 93\n\nEmulating the Hunter archetype means accepting your place as a bulwark between civilization and the terrors of the wilderness. As you walk the Hunter's path, you learn specialized techniques for fighting the threats you face, from rampaging ogres and hordes of orcs to towering giants and terrifying dragons."},
